# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
# bash reads a CRLF script literally: `set -euo pipefail\r` parses as the
# option name "pipefail\r", which fails with "invalid option name" and
# takes the whole build down. This only surfaced on `vercel --prod` from a
# Windows machine (which uploads the local working copy); git-triggered
# builds were fine because the repo itself stores LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# SQL migrations are pasted into Supabase's SQL editor and read on Linux
# hosts; no reason to carry CRLF into either.
*.sql text eol=lf
